ly all samples fall under the  rules for qualifying as dea exempt  materials  which allows us to ship these samples  nationwide and internationally with few  exceptions  pass fail criteria is determined by the  iso 17043 pt manufacturers  and while some tests are graded by  standard mean others are graded by known  value  which is metrologically traceable this  is also determined by the iso 17043  pt manufacturer and can change as more  historical performance data is gathered  unlike other areas of analytics  currently  at the time of this presentation field  of proficiency  tables known as fopt tables which  provides specific guidance for  establishing passing criteria  and test design do not exist for the  cannabis industry  by leveraging the input of our advisory  panel our customers  and ever changing regulations we  continually advocate  for new and approved tests that are  relevant to the needs of the industry  this graph recently generated by new  frontiers data  illustrates the expansion of the emerald  test ilcpt program since 2014  and while i recognize that this slide  may be difficult to read  what is important to know is that over  time we have continued to add new tests  and matrices  to address the industry's analytical  needs  all right so let's get to the data  already how it's delivered and what does  it mean  initially you will receive an individual  performance report  for each test in which you have  participated this is generally what your  auditors will review  after we've completed a statistical  analysis of the testing round you will  receive a full report  with a data summary in this example for  pesticides  and this is from the spring of 2000 2020  and this is just a little subsection of  the pesticides here  a statistical summary was provided and  here you can see that more challenging  analytes such as abamectin which is  circled in red  will have a higher standard deviation  than those analytes easier to  identify such as boscolin which is  circled in green  z-score data was also provided which  easily identifies standard deviation  results  by color  also provided resize score graphs and  gaussian  normal distribution plots the way data  is visualized  and tracking this data historically can  provide insights into the challenges  and improvements both in performance and  analytics  and the design of a test  so who should participate in proficiency  testing as i already noted  any lab seeking iso 17025 accreditation  and obviously if you are a lab required  by state regulations to do so  but also in-house quality control and r  d lab should participate to ensure that  your analytics are in alignment with the  industry  we are also seeing an increase in  equipment providers participating to  ensure that the equipment and methods  they are providing to the industry  are capable of providing the analytics  required  so let's touch upon some brief  highlights from the most recent fall  2020 round of the emerald test ilc pt  program it is worth noting that the labs  were all very responsive during the test  period  even though there was a global pandemic  potency performance is solid  but in all cannabinoid tests cbn cbd and  cba had  significantly higher standard deviations  than other potency  analytes which indicates that these are  more challenging  to accurately quantify terpene analysis  continues to be the most challenging  test with  beta-caryophyllene providing or proving  to be the most difficult analyte  in some microbio biological tests we  increase the number of samples in the  test and the pass rate remained the same  but with aspergillus molds the panel  increased from three samples to ten and  the pass rate increased by five percent  which was unexpected  with the mycotoxins test the pass rate  was 2 percent better than historic  performance  and for pesticides the average recovery  of the certified value improved from 88  percent to 96 percent  in reviewing participation we had a  total of 123 different cannabis and or  hemp  testing facilities enrolled for the fall  and will test  representing 30 states and 8 foreign  countries  this is the 13th consecutive round that  the number of participants has increased  and while some labs are unable to submit  results it is noteworthy  that 610 pts were entered for review  which culminated in 511 emerald test  badges being awarded  it was also noted that this round  continued a significant trend in the  diversity of enterprises participating  in the emerald test  the program is now being utilized by  regulatory bodies  equipment manufacturers method  development entities  cultivators extraction businesses and  consumable product creators  fall 2020 results indicate that matrix  does influence accuracy as represented  in this bar graph  illustrating the potency results for  both hemp bud  and hemp oil potency results have shown  consistent improvement over time  with an average pass rate of 89 percent  over the history of the test  additionally labs have demonstrated  exceptional results across other  matrices  including gummies beverages and hard  candy  the combined pass rate was 97 percent  the graph here illustrates that gummies  present a greater analytical challenge  for potency analysis than beverage or  hard candy  we just completed enrollment for our  spring 2021 round  so here's the summary of the enrollment  we had 139 individual labs enroll  representing 12 countries for a total of  760  tests so the enroll is comprised of  cannabis testing labs  hemp testing labs instrument instrument  manufacturers  government labs and cannabis product  manufacturers  so let's talk about some key insights  and what might be coming next  according to new frontiers data growth  in the cannabis sales  is expected to more than double in the  next four years  recent legalization activities in  several states  the influence those will have on the  surrounding states combined with the  increased  acceptance of the need for regulatory  oversight  and testing requirements positions the  lab testing market for exponential  growth within the next few years  in this highly competitive market it  will be more critical than ever  for labs to differentiate from one  another through accreditation and proof  of analytical capability  we are seeing a notable increase in  manufacturers and cultivators embracing  and investing  in in-house testing capabilities and we  expect to see this trend continue as we  move toward  improved processes such as good  manufacturing  practices otherwise known as gmp of  which testing is an important component  this will influence domestic and  international trade and thus requiring a  greater demand for quality analytics  looking to the future cbd is a  hot topic right now and pun intended the  highly restrictive 0.3 percent threshold  for thc content in hump derived products  reinforces urgency for precise  quantification capabilities  it is still uncertain how and to what  extent this market segment will be  effectively regulated as a reply as it  applies to consumer safety  and next i'll talk briefly about delta  eight this is a rising player in the cbd  hunt market  in this presentation i'm hesitant to  navigate the legal framework of delta  eight  similar to a stormy day it appears to be  dark and gray  but there is much controversy  surrounding the popular cannabinoid  typically derived from hemp-based cbd  what i can address is that there is an  issue in the testing industry  where some labs are unable to accurately  differentiate between delta 8 and delta  9 in their analysis  we are working with our suppliers to  help address this problem by delivering  a delta 8 delta 9 proficiency test  before the end of the month so so what  are the challenges we continue to face  that pertain to proficiency tests first  cannabinoid tests must meet  qualification for dea exempt materials  this means that they must be below one  milligram per mill in thc concentration  we are also unable to ship samples in a  solid matrix above  0.3 thc across state lines  and this is unlikely to change until we  see some form of federal legalization  the exception to this may be if you have  a dea license to handle schedule 1 drugs  the vast variability across state  regulations makes it difficult to create  tests that are relevant for all markets  also as noted earlier we are a young  industry and still lack enough  historical data to  to determine passing criteria is  typically referenced by fopt  fopt tables and finally we continue to  work toward  customer education and as to the value  of proficiency testing programs and what  they provide to the industry  participation in these in these programs  goes well beyond  just a marketing opportunity  participation contributes to the overall  advancement of cannabis science  like to acknowledge my references  and thank you i truly appreciate your  attention and interest  and a huge thank you to the lab roots  organization for allowing me to  participate today  and for all they do to support the  cannabis analytical space
 

